#: server_ui/templates/about.html:12
msgid "About Helios Voting"
msgstr "Acerca de Helios Voting"

#: server_ui/templates/about.html:15
msgid ""
"Helios is a non-partisan organization led by <a href=\"http://"
"ben.adida.net\">Ben Adida</a>."
msgstr ""
"Helios es una organización no partidista dirigida por <a href=\"http://"
"ben.adida.net\">Ben Adida</a>."

#: server_ui/templates/about.html:21
msgid "Code Contributors"
msgstr "Colaboradores del código"

#: server_ui/templates/about.html:27
msgid "Advisors"
msgstr "Asesores"

#: server_ui/templates/about.html:32
msgid ""
"Jim is a business executive, entrepreneur, and thought leader on big\n"
"data, privacy, security, and voting systems. He’s founded companies,\n"
"defined vision and strategy, led teams, developed technology, and\n"
"built products."
msgstr ""
"Jim es un ejecutivo de negocios, emprendedor y referente en materia de\n"
"big data, privacidad, seguridad y sistemas de votación. Ha fundado "
"empresas,\n"
"definido visión y estrategia, liderado equipos, desarrollado tecnología y\n"
"creado productos."

#: server_ui/templates/about.html:38
msgid ""
"Currently, Jim is Vice President of Products at Metanautix, a big data\n"
"analytics startup. He also serves on the The Department of Homeland\n"
"Security (DHS) Data Privacy and Integrity Advisory Committee (DPIAC)\n"
"providing advice at the request of the Secretary of Homeland Security\n"
"and the DHS Chief Privacy Officer."
msgstr ""
"Actualmente, Jim es Vicepresidente de Productos en Metanautix, una startup\n"
"de análisis de big data. También forma parte del Comité Asesor de "
"Privacidad\n"
"e Integridad de Datos (DPIAC) del Departamento de Seguridad Nacional (DHS),\n"
"asesorando a solicitud del Secretario de Seguridad Nacional\n"
"y del Director de Privacidad del DHS."

#: server_ui/templates/about.html:42 server_ui/templates/about.html:50
msgid "more"
msgstr "más"

#: server_ui/templates/about.html:50
msgid ""
"Lawrence Lessig is the Director of the Edmond J. Safra Foundation Center for "
"Ethics at Harvard University, and a Professor of Law at Harvard Law School. "
"For much of his academic career, Lessig has focused on law and technology, "
"especially as it affects copyright. His current academic work addresses the "
"question of “institutional corruption” — roughly, influences within an "
"economy of influence that weaken the effectiveness of an institution, or "
"weaken public trust. His current work at the EJ Safra Lab oversees a 5 year "
"research project addressing institutional corruption in a number of "
"institutional contexts."
msgstr ""
"Lawrence Lessig es el Director del Centro de Ética de la Fundación Edmond J. "
"Safra en la Universidad de Harvard, y Profesor de Derecho en la Facultad de "
"Derecho de Harvard. Durante gran parte de su carrera académica, Lessig se ha "
"enfocado en el derecho y la tecnología, especialmente en lo relativo a los "
"derechos de autor. Su trabajo académico actual aborda la cuestión de la "
"«corrupción institucional» —a grandes rasgos, influencias dentro de una "
"economía de influencia que debilitan la eficacia de una institución o la "
"confianza pública. Su trabajo actual en el EJ Safra Lab supervisa un "
"proyecto de investigación de 5 años sobre la corrupción institucional en "
"diversos contextos institucionales."

#: server_ui/templates/about.html:58
msgid ""
"Dr. Benaloh is Senior Cryptographer at Microsoft Research and an elected "
"director of the International Association for Cryptologic Research. He "
"earned his S.B degree from the Massachusetts Institute of Technology and "
"M.S., M.Phil., and Ph.D. degrees from Yale University where his 1987 "
"doctoral dissertation, Verifiable Secret-Ballot Elections, introduced the "
"use of homomorphic encryption to enable end-to-end verifiable election "
"technologies. Dr. Benaloh’s numerious research publications in cryptography "
"and voting have pioneered new tehnologies including the “cast or cancel” "
"paradigm which brings voters into the verification process with minimal "
"burden. He has served on the program committees of dozens of cryptography "
"and election-related conferences and workshops and is a frequent speaker on "
"the history, development, and mechanisms behind verifiable voting."
msgstr ""
"El Dr. Benaloh es Criptógrafo Sénior en Microsoft Research y director electo "
"de la Asociación Internacional de Investigación Criptológica. Obtuvo su "
"título de grado en el Instituto Tecnológico de Massachusetts y sus títulos "
"de maestría, M.Phil. y doctorado en la Universidad de Yale, donde su tesis "
"doctoral de 1987, Verifiable Secret-Ballot Elections, introdujo el uso del "
"cifrado homomórfico para posibilitar tecnologías electorales verificables de "
"extremo a extremo. Las numerosas publicaciones de investigación del Dr. "
"Benaloh en criptografía y votación han sido pioneras en nuevas tecnologías, "
"incluido el paradigma «emitir o cancelar», que involucra a los votantes en "
"el proceso de verificación con una carga mínima. Ha formado parte de los "
"comités de programa de decenas de conferencias y talleres relacionados con "
"criptografía y elecciones, y es un conferenciante habitual sobre la "
"historia, el desarrollo y los mecanismos de la votación verificable."

#: server_ui/templates/about.html:66
msgid ""
"Dr. Neff is the author of several ground-breaking contributions to the study "
"of computer algorithms, specifically as they apply to voting protocols. At "
"VoteHere, where he was CTO, Dr. Neff created the first ballot mixing and "
"anonymization technique efficient enough for practical use, developed a new "
"ballot representation which allows for a reduction in ballot size by several "
"factors with privacy intact, and led the technical vision of the VoteHere "
"election product. Dr. Neff regularly serves on the program committees of top "
"voting conferences and holds a PhD in Mathematics from Princeton University."
msgstr ""
"El Dr. Neff es autor de varias contribuciones pioneras al estudio de los "
"algoritmos informáticos, en particular en su aplicación a los protocolos de "
"votación. En VoteHere, donde fue CTO, el Dr. Neff creó la primera técnica de "
"mezcla y anonimización de papeletas suficientemente eficiente para uso "
"práctico, desarrolló una nueva representación de papeleta que permite "
"reducir su tamaño en varios factores manteniendo la privacidad intacta, y "
"lideró la visión técnica del producto electoral de VoteHere. El Dr. Neff "
"forma parte habitualmente de los comités de programa de las principales "
"conferencias sobre votación y posee un doctorado en Matemáticas de la "
"Universidad de Princeton."

#: server_ui/templates/about.html:74
msgid ""
"Olivier Pereira is a research associate of the Belgian science foundation "
"F.R.S.-FNRS and an associate professor at Université catholique de Louvain. "
"His research interests lie in the area of cryptography and distributed "
"computing, addressing the issue of enabling people to jointly realize tasks "
"in a secure way. He has been leading the development, integration and "
"deployment of Helios in several large scale elections, and gave invited "
"presentations and keynote talks about verifiable elections in a dozen of "
"leading institutions around the world. He is a co-author of the Bevoting "
"study on electronic voting systems produced for the Belgian Federal and "
"Regional Administrations."
msgstr ""
"Olivier Pereira es investigador asociado de la fundación científica belga "
"F.R.S.-FNRS y profesor asociado en la Universidad Católica de Lovaina. Sus "
"intereses de investigación se centran en la criptografía y la computación "
"distribuida, abordando el problema de permitir que las personas realicen "
"tareas conjuntas de manera segura. Ha liderado el desarrollo, la integración "
"y la implementación de Helios en varias elecciones de gran escala, y ha "
"ofrecido presentaciones invitadas y conferencias magistrales sobre "
"elecciones verificables en una decena de instituciones líderes de todo el "
"mundo. Es coautor del estudio Bevoting sobre sistemas de votación "
"electrónica elaborado para las administraciones federales y regionales de "
"Bélgica."

#: server_ui/templates/about.html:80
msgid ""
"Dan Wallach is an associate professor in the Department of Computer Science "
"at Rice University in Houston, Texas and is the director of NSF’s ACCURATE "
"(A Center for Correct, Usable, Reliable, Auditable and Transparent "
"Elections). His research involves computer security and the issues of "
"building secure and robust software systems for the Internet. He has "
"testified about voting security issues before government bodies in the U.S., "
"Mexico, and the European Union, has served as an expert witness in a number "
"of voting technology lawsuits, and participated in California’s “top-to-"
"bottom” audit of its voting systems."
msgstr ""
"Dan Wallach es profesor asociado del Departamento de Ciencias de la "
"Computación de la Universidad Rice en Houston, Texas, y director de ACCURATE "
"(A Center for Correct, Usable, Reliable, Auditable and Transparent "
"Elections) de la NSF. Su investigación abarca la seguridad informática y los "
"problemas de construir sistemas de software seguros y robustos para "
"Internet. Ha testificado sobre cuestiones de seguridad electoral ante "
"organismos gubernamentales en Estados Unidos, México y la Unión Europea, ha "
"actuado como testigo experto en varias demandas relacionadas con tecnología "
"de votación, y participó en la auditoría «de arriba abajo» de los sistemas "
"de votación de California."

